WHAT CHANGED IN THIS REBUILD (HARD POLICY compliance)
  OLD (BANNED): lifted lib/rexml trees baked into ruby:2.7 + in-process `docker compose
  run` calling parse.rb -> REXML::Document.new. That triggered the library IN-PROCESS.
  NEW: REAL published REXML *as bundled in real Ruby* (official ruby:2.1.3/2.1.4/2.1.5
  images, bundled REXML 3.1.7.3) inside a REAL Ruby web app (WEBrick, stdlib 1.3.1). The
  DoS is triggered by an EXTERNAL HTTP request (POST /parse, body = attacker XML) and
  measured as SERVER-SIDE latency. No lifted source, no in-process call.

